    "body":  "fixes #820 \r\n\r\n## What this changes\r\n\r\nAdds the Sentry connector to Switch\u0027s connection catalog, allowing agents to inspect Sentry issues, events, stack traces, and releases through Sentry\u0027s remote MCP server at `https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp`.\r\n\r\n### Why `adapter: api_key` over OAuth\r\nIssue #820 asks to prefer OAuth with dynamic client registration (DCR) where available and explain the chosen shape in the PR:\r\n1. Sentry\u0027s MCP server at `mcp.sentry.dev` supports DCR, but it is built on Cloudflare Workers OAuth Provider and issues downstream worker tokens (`userId:grantId:secret`).\r\n2. `mcp.sentry.dev` does not provide an OIDC `/userinfo` endpoint or an RFC 7662 token introspection endpoint. It only exposes a JSON-RPC `whoami` tool over MCP.\r\n3. Upstream `https://sentry.io/api/0/users/me/` rejects downstream worker tokens with HTTP 401, so Switch cannot complete its REST identity verification (`auth.identity`).\r\n4. Sentry MCP natively supports Sentry User Auth Tokens through the `Authorization: Sentry-Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` header scheme.\r\n5. Sentry User Auth Tokens are validated directly against `GET https://sentry.io/api/0/users/me/` (`account_id: id`, `label: email`), which matches Switch\u0027s `adapter: api_key` pattern (same as Datadog).\r\n\r\n### Included changes\r\n- Added catalog definition `core/switch_core/connections/catalog/sentry/connection.yaml`\r\n- Added agent skill `core/switch_core/connections/catalog/sentry/skill/SKILL.md` with guidelines on narrow queries, issue inspection, and data privacy\r\n- Vendored Sentry mark at `console/apps/switch-console-desktop/src/assets/images/connections/sentry.svg` with `fill=\"currentColor\"`\r\n- Added license entry to `console/apps/switch-console-desktop/src/assets/images/connections/NOTICE.md`\r\n- Registered brand color in `console/apps/switch-console-desktop/src/renderer/features/switch-servers/connection-icon.tsx` (`#362D59` with dark theme fallback)\r\n- Added Sentry to `console/packages/agent-providers/src/host/service-notices.ts`\r\n- Added Sentry catalog and header tests to `core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py`\r\n\r\n## How it was tested\r\n\r\n1. Ran catalog loader unit tests:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   PYTHONPATH=core pytest --noconftest core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py\r\n   ```\r\n   Output: `128 passed in 1.71s` (verifies catalog schema, enabled services, token policy, and MCP request headers).\r\n\r\n2. Ran connection icon test suite:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   cd console \u0026\u0026 pnpm --filter @switch-console/desktop test connection-icon.test.ts\r\n   ```\r\n   Output: `38 passed in 935ms` (verifies logo presence, SVG attributes, and NOTICE.md entries).\r\n\r\n3. Ran TypeScript checks across console packages:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   cd console \u0026\u0026 pnpm -r run typecheck\r\n   ```\r\n   Output: `Done` across all 8 workspace packages with zero errors.\r\n\r\n4. Tested live MCP endpoint authentication:\r\n   Sent a JSON-RPC ping to `https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp` using `Authorization: Sentry-Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` and `Accept: application/json, text/event-stream`.\r\n   The endpoint returned `HTTP/2 200 OK` with SSE payload `data: {\"result\":{},\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1}`.\r\n\r\n5. Tested live identity endpoint:\r\n   Queried `GET https://sentry.io/api/0/users/me/` without credentials; received `HTTP/2 401 Unauthorized` with `www-authenticate: Bearer realm=\"api\"`, confirming the endpoint validates Bearer tokens for identity mapping.",
